{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790481932,"nonce":"KMBeasKTgwetXp0uGzyQB6/wRhY=","title":"Compiler: a constant-index check on a list that does not change in a loop is repeated every iteration","message":"nbody_modified's advance reads v1[0], v1[1], v1[2] inside the pair\nloop; each access still compares the constant index against the list's\nlength and branches to the failing arm every iteration, although the\nlist (and so the answer) is the same for the whole inner loop once its\nlength is read before it. Bounds versioning does not take these (the\nindex is not the counter), and LICM hoists the compare but not the\nbranch.\n\nFix direction: unswitch on a loop-invariant condition whose false arm\nleaves the loop (test once in the preheader, run the loop without the\ncheck), or fold `ge c, len` for constant c against a length known to be\nlarger. Separately, sign_fold misses `lt %p, 0` when %p is a\nsingle-incoming phi of the counter in a non-header block: such phi\nresults have no entry in func.values, and non_negative() seeds only\nvalues it finds there.","files":null}]}